(:card "core/lang" :purpose "how to write ASL: syntax, effects, matching, records" :rules ("file: (module NAME :x [exported names] :i [(pkg/module :a alias)]) on line 1, then column-0 items: fn, schema, enum; ; starts a line comment" "call an import as alias/name, e.g. :i [(asl-json/json :a j)] then (j/jsonParse s); builtins need no import" "fn header is one unparenthesised line at column 0: fn name a: Int64 b: String -> Bool; the body is one expression on the indented lines below; the header has no closing paren" "a fn that calls an effectful builtin (println, file*, dir*, process*, envGet) or any ! fn is effectful; ! is optional, the checker infers the effect either way (EFFECT-INFER); a manifest.asn with :pure true turns an inferred, unmarked effect into ERR_EFFECT_UNMARKED naming the call chain, otherwise it is never an error" "types: Int64 Float64 Bool String Bytes Unit (List T) (Map K V) (Option T) (Result T E) (Pair A B); Int and Str are aliases; Unit value is ()" "every call is prefix: (+ a b) (* a b) (- a b) (/ a b) (mod a b) (= a b) (< a b) (and a b c) (or a b) (not a); = compares strings and lists too" "(let [(a 1) (b (+ a 1))] body); later bindings see earlier ones; (do e1 e2 last) sequences effects" "(if c then else) always has an else; (cond (c1 v1) (c2 v2) (else v))" "(mt x ((some v) e1) ((none) e2)) matches Option; ((ok v) ..) ((err e) ..) matches Result; arms are (pattern expr), patterns one level deep: ctor with names or _, a literal, _ or a bare name; nest a second mt for inner values" "lambda: (fn [(x Int64)] -> Int64 (* x 2)); (map f xs) (filter f xs) (fold (fn [(acc B) (x A)] -> B ..) init xs); loops are recursion" "lists: [1 2 3] or (list 1 2 3); (listHead xs) (listGet xs i) return Option; strings: (str \"n=\" 3) concatenates and renders numbers" "schema: (schema P (:f x Int64)); build (P :x 1), read p.x, copy with change (with p :x 2); enum: enum S then indented ctor lines (circle r: Int64), build (circle 2), match ((circle r) ..)" "values are immutable; Map ops return a new map: (mapSet m k v) (mapGet m k) -> Option (mapGetOr m k dflt)" "names are camelCase whole words; predicates end in ? (listEmpty? xs); effectful fns usually end in !" "a test module exports fn ! runTests -> Bool that runs (assert cond \"msg\") forms and returns true; asl test FILE runs it; a runnable entry is fn ! main args: (List String) -> (Result Int64 String) run by asl run FILE args") :pit ((:result "returns (Result T E): handle both (ok v) and (err e), or (resultOr r dflt)") (:option "returns (Option T): handle (some v) and (none), or (optionOr o dflt)") (:effect "effectful: inferred from the call, not from a missing !; only a :pure manifest.asn turns this into an error") (:ctor "enum constructor: build (ctor args), match ((ctor a b) ..) one level deep") (:record "schema: build (Name :field v ...), read x.field, update (with x :field v)") (:variadic "takes any number of arguments")) :heal "asl heal FILE repairs common slips in place" :example "(module asl-know/examples/coreLang :x [Point Shape area describe total selfTest] :i [])\n\n(schema Point (:f x Int64) (:f y Int64))\n\nenum Shape\n  (circle r: Int64)\n  (rect w: Int64 h: Int64)\n\nfn area s: Shape -> Int64\n  (match s\n    ((circle r) (* 3 (* r r)))\n    ((rect w h) (* w h)))\n\nfn describe n: Int64 -> String\n  (cond\n    ((< n 0) \"negative\")\n    ((= n 0) \"zero\")\n    (else (str \"positive \" n)))\n\nfn total xs: (List Int64) -> Int64\n  (let [(evens (filter (fn [(x Int64)] -> Bool (= (mod x 2) 0)) xs))\n        (sum (fold (fn [(acc Int64) (x Int64)] -> Int64 (+ acc x)) 0 evens))\n        (first (optionOr (listHead xs) 0))]\n    (if (> sum 0) (+ sum first) first))")
